{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>I heard, and my stomach trembled</b> — because of lack of food." "The sense of <b>לקול</b> [at the sound] is: because of this sound." "<b>My lips quivered</b> — that one strikes against the other, from the root of מצלתים [cymbals]." "<b>And he mentioned \"my lips\"</b> because the mouth is the gateway of food." "<b>Rot enters my bones</b> — for when the food that nourishes the flesh ceases, then the bone rots." "<b>And beneath me I tremble</b> — in my place, in the land of Israel." "<b>That I might rest</b> — I thought I would find rest when the grain arrives, if the enemy comes." "<b>To advance against the people, our attacker</b> — יגודנו [our attacker] is a marauding band, and behold the matter is reversed."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:18.105196980Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}